REUTERS BREAKING NEWS

Fed cuts interest rates by 50 bps in emergency move

WASHINGTON, Aug 12 (Reuters) - The U.S. Federal Reserve cut interest rates
by half a percentage point on Wednesday in its first unscheduled policy
action since the pandemic, moving to shore up confidence as credit spreads
widened sharply.

